If you want the DevTeam to change their organization, you're simply 
adressing the wrong audience if you write on rgrn.  If you want 
the rgrn community to Take Things Into Their Own Hands, you need 
a heck of a lot more reasons than a vague 'would benefit'.  The 
balance of power as is is "the DevTeam decides everything about 
the official nethack code"; to change this, you'd need quite some 
inertia.  

If you want to improve the coordination of nh patching, you could 
try and give Patchhack a helping hand.  Or build a patch database 
on your own, or start such a project and ask for helping hands 
here.  But I don't see much value in trying to change the DevTeam's 
Way Of Doing Things <polemics=on> just because they don't spin off 
nh 2 -- Back To Gehennom Or How Dumb It Is To Forget The Stupid 
